# R1 research device helper build artifacts (gitignored *.so already)
src/saccade/perception/eval/_cuda/libr1_bridge_replay.build.json

# Agent/session review scratch dumps (session scratchpad lives in /tmp)
scratchpad/

# Sealed research evidence is inventoried byte-exactly by each archive's own
# checksum manifest, so the generic `runs/` and `*.log` rules above must never
# silently drop archive members: a partially committed archive fails its own
# completeness check, and the most diagnostic file (a failed child's stderr) is
# exactly the one those rules would eat. Re-include the directory before its
# contents — git cannot re-include a file inside an excluded directory.
!docs/modules/semantic/research/evidence/**/runs/
!docs/modules/semantic/research/evidence/**/*.log
# A measurement child runs under a closed HOME/TMPDIR/XDG_CACHE_HOME inside its
# own run directory, so the compiler caches it materialises (Triton's
# `cuda_utils…so`) are inventoried archive members like any other. The generic
# `*.so` rule above would drop exactly those seven files and break the closure.
!docs/modules/semantic/research/evidence/**/*.so

# AP-3 asset inventory: a workspace-local projection of gitignored asset roots.
# Committing it would make a view of an 82 GB workspace look like a repo fact,
# and it must stay out of docs/ because build_master_map rglobs that tree.
.provenance/

# Local runtime linker path helper, sourced (not executed) before running the
# CUDA/TensorRT pipeline: `source setup_env.sh`. It is untracked because every
# entry it exports is a machine-local absolute path — the interpreter version is
# baked into the `.venv/lib/python3.12/...` segments and the toolkit prefix is
# `/opt/cuda/lib64` — so committing one developer's copy would hand everyone
# else a path list that silently resolves to nothing.
#
# It is not part of any build- or run-identity attestation. H0/H2 measurement
# children run under a closed HOME/TMPDIR/XDG_CACHE_HOME and record their own
# runtime inputs; a tracked shell entry point would add an environment source
# that no attestation covers, which is worse than no entry point at all.
#
# To reproduce it after a fresh clone (this is the whole file):
#
#     #!/usr/bin/env bash
#     SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"
#     export LD_LIBRARY_PATH="${SCRIPT_DIR}/build:\
#     ${SCRIPT_DIR}/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/tensorrt_libs:\
#     ${SCRIPT_DIR}/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/nvidia/cuda_runtime/lib:\
#     /opt/cuda/lib64${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:${LD_LIBRARY_PATH}}"
#
# Substitute the real `python3.N` of `.venv` and the real CUDA prefix. Symptom
# when it is missing or stale: an import or a native call dies on a missing
# `libcublas*`/`libnvinfer*` shared object even though the wheels are installed,
# because the loader never searches the wheel-private lib directories.
setup_env.sh
